# Trivy vulnerability ignore list
# --------------------------------
# CVEs listed here are accepted risks documented in .security-exceptions.yml.
# Only ignore CVEs that have no available fix or are blocked by a known
# dependency constraint. Review before each expiry date.

# pyasn1 CVEs — transitive dependency of python-jose which pins pyasn1<0.5.0.
# Cannot be upgraded until python-jose is replaced with pyjwt/joserfc.
# Our JWT implementation uses HS256 only and does not process untrusted ASN.1.
# Reviewed: 2026-08-07. Expires: 2026-10-31.
CVE-2026-30922
CVE-2026-59884
CVE-2026-59885
CVE-2026-59886

# jaraco.context — pip build tool, not imported or used at runtime.
# The path traversal vulnerability requires a malicious package archive during
# install, which is mitigated by our pinned requirements.txt with hashed deps.
# Will be resolved when pip upgrades its bundled version.
# Reviewed: 2026-08-07. Expires: 2026-10-31.
CVE-2026-23949

# wheel — pip build tool, not a runtime dependency.
# The privilege escalation requires running 'pip wheel' with untrusted input,
# which we do not do. Our images are built from a pinned requirements.txt.
# Will be resolved when the base image ships a patched pip.
# Reviewed: 2026-08-07. Expires: 2026-10-31.
CVE-2026-24049
